You'd use the same pattern you already have for maintenance mode: a settings table row checked and cached per request.

The flow: Deploy the rebuilt checkout code (it's already in checkout-v2.js), add a row to your settings table (`INSERT INTO settings (key, value) VALUES ('checkout_v2_enabled', false)`), then gate the routing on that flag:

```javascript
// In app.js
app.use(async (req, res, next) => {
  if (req.path.startsWith("/checkout")) {
    if (Date.now() - checkoutFlagCache.at > 15000) {
      const rows = await db.query("SELECT value FROM settings WHERE key = 'checkout_v2_enabled'");
      checkoutFlagCache = { value: rows.length && rows[0].value === true, at: Date.now() };
    }
    return checkoutFlagCache.value 
      ? require("./routes/checkout-v2")(req, res, next)
      : require("./routes/checkout")(req, res, next);
  }
  next();
});
```

When ready to activate, just `UPDATE settings SET value = true WHERE key = 'checkout_v2_enabled'` from your database, and within 15 seconds all requests see the new version. No deploy needed. You can also toggle it back just as fast if there's a problem.
